# promise: #685
# Edge to edge, a double click on the toolbar's empty part zooms the window as with the margin around the page (the
# toolbar-double-click-zoom scenario). It did nothing there (GitHub #685, neolytic, 0.1.54). The double click is a
# real one, through the window server as a mouse sends it (scripts/hid-click/click.m): edge to edge the toolbar sits
# in the hidden title bar's band at the window's top.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true, "edgeToEdgeContent": true}
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=zoom
wait 2
cra://debug?mainFrame=100,100,1000,700
wait 1
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
click toolbar-empty double
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbarZoom=real
expect-log toolbar zoom real: zoomed=1 grew=1
